@startuml 05d-sequence-artifact-flow
title Artifact flow — publish on cluster A, consume on cluster B

skinparam defaultFontName Menlo

actor "Operator A" as OpA
participant "sphinx.sh\n(on cluster A head)" as ShA
participant "MinIO" as Min
participant "Postgres registry" as PG
participant "sphinx.sh\n(on cluster B head)" as ShB
actor "Operator B" as OpB

== Publish (after training completes on cluster A) ==

OpA -> ShA : sphinx publish experiments/001
ShA -> ShA : compute sha256 of:\n  model_parameters/<db>.cd_cont_N/\n  etc/sphinx_train.cfg\n  etc/<db>.dic, etc/<db>.filler
ShA -> Min : put experiments/001.cfg\n  key=sha256(cfg)
ShA -> Min : put model tar\n  key=sha256(model)
ShA -> Min : put dict+phones\n  key=sha256(dict)
ShA -> PG : INSERT INTO experiments\n  (name, owner, origin=A,\n   cfg_hash, model_hash, dict_hash,\n   created_at, wer=NULL)
ShA --> OpA : published; hash = <model_hash>

== Consume (later, on cluster B) ==

OpB -> ShB : sphinx pull <experiment_name>\n    --decode-corpus librispeech/test-clean
ShB -> PG : SELECT * FROM experiments\n  WHERE name=<...>
PG --> ShB : row (model_hash, dict_hash, cfg_hash)
ShB -> Min : HEAD by cfg_hash / model_hash / dict_hash
alt object missing
    Min --> ShB : 404
    ShB --> OpB : ERROR: artifact missing\n(did cluster A's GC purge it?)
else present
    ShB -> Min : GET model tar  → experiments/042/model_parameters/
    ShB -> Min : GET cfg        → experiments/042/etc/
    ShB -> Min : GET dict       → experiments/042/etc/
    ShB --> OpB : materialized as experiments/042 on cluster B

    OpB -> ShB : sphinx decode experiments/042
    note right of ShB
      Decode uses the Phase-3 sbatch --array
      local to cluster B. No cross-cluster
      scheduling needed; only the artifacts
      travel, not the compute.
    end note
    ShB -> Min : put decode result (hash)
    ShB -> PG : UPDATE experiments SET\n  decode_wer=...  WHERE id=...
    ShB --> OpB : WER X.XX%
end

note right of PG
  Registry row is the shared "what models exist"
  index. MinIO is the bag-of-bytes. Together
  they let a new cluster (or dropout node)
  self-serve without operator scp.
end note

@enduml
